            <ArticleTitle>[Ataralgesia with nalbuphine-midazolam instead of fentanyl-midazolam analgesia. Anesthesia and the postoperative control of pain. A preliminary report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>34-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nalbuphine-midazolam ataractanalgesia has been studied in anaesthesia and postoperative analgesia. Attention has been applied to the efficiency, pharmacological activity, side effects, adverse reactions of nalbuphine as a fentanyl substitute. Preliminary results show that nalbuphine could be used safely as anaesthesia component and as postoperative analgetic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
